    "problem": "Understanding past Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation (AMOC) shifts is limited because proxy records from individual locations provide conflicting data on the timing and magnitude of these changes, preventing a coherent, basin-wide reconstruction of past climate events.",
    "method": "This study proposes a method of compiling and synthesizing new and existing sedimentary 231Pa/230Th proxy records on a common chronology, and evaluating them for geochemical controls, to produce a spatially coherent reconstruction of past Atlantic Ocean circulation changes.",
    "task": "This paper's task is to reconstruct Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation (AMOC) changes during the last deglaciation by synthesizing sedimentary 231Pa/230Th proxy records to determine the timing and drivers of abrupt climate transitions, particularly the relationship between ocean circulation and melting ice sheets.",
